":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State an explicit, tested rollback for the fix to autodeploy.sh (e.g. how a revert commit re-installs the prior deploy loop and reaches the box) so a bad fix to the deploy mechanism itself can be undone quickly.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan states 'This recovery is an operator break-glass, not a fix.'","Fix candidates ('re-exec the script...', 'separate install sources from perform rolls into two ticks') alter the core deploy loop; no revert/rollback of the fix is described.","AC only guards against a re-exec LOOP, not against a wedged deploy loop caused by the fix."],"finding":"The plan does not specify a rollback/reversibility path for the FIX itself (the re-exec / delta-content / split-tick change to autodeploy.sh). The documented 'Recovery performed' is a break-glass for the incident, not a tested revert of the shipped fix — and the fix modifies the very mechanism that deploys everything, so a bad fix could wedge all future rolls.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb290a6b1cbe263c1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Recovery performed' section / Investigation notes","norm_id":"ncd0fbc0afe57619a","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance criterion describing how reverting the fix commit restores prior autodeploy behavior end-to-end, and confirm the revert path does not itself require the buggy one-tick-late behavior to install.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Require the repro and post-fix tests to assert on the ACTUAL running/constructed container configuration (env vars + bind), explicitly NOT on the content of the installed autodeploy.sh file, so the test cannot pass on the same false marker that hid the incident.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Incident: '/opt/rebar/infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh did contain the new flags and bind' while 'The live container ... had none of the 3 env vars and no bind.'","AC #2 says 'asserting on the resulting container configuration' (container-level, good), but AC #1 ('a change ... is not reflected in the container created during the same tick') does not pin the assertion target — a grep of the installed script would pass while proving nothing."],"finding":"AC #1/#2 risk being satisfied by a self-authored-oracle / source-grep that greps the installed autodeploy.sh for the new flags — which is exactly the marker that LIED in the incident (the file was updated while the container was not). The plan should explicitly forbid asserting on installed-script content and require assertion on live/actual container configuration.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f981d93225387cc2f","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria items 1 and 2","norm_id":"n6506a3146ed9ae88","priority":0.2063,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Amend AC #1 and #4 to state the oracle is the created container's config/inspect output (or the exact docker run invocation the roll performs), and that source-content of the installed script is not an acceptable proxy.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"f482553d7cd7a153","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["bd0698ac9130e0ea",4550],"description_boxes":["399141be1d30ac26",0],"file_impact":["122fbf2e39918416",3],"ticket_id":["513f02438ad817cf",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":286960,"cache_write_tokens":244336,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":3736.5,"input_tokens":551921,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms